# Account closure is irreversible. Use a disposable local account with posts/comments.
# Current policy preserves contributions and shows Deleted user; credentials/name/bio are removed.
# Owned communities must be transferred first (409); no transfer endpoint is added by this slice.
# Sign in using auth.http, then fetch authenticated CSRF and copy it here. Keep the cookie jar.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7240
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_AUTHENTICATED_CSRF_TOKEN
@password = REPLACE_WITH_DISPOSABLE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD
@participantId = REPLACE_WITH_DISPOSABLE_PARTICIPANT_GUID
@nodeId = REPLACE_WITH_A_POST_OWNED_BY_THIS_ACCOUNT

### D1. Capture session participantId before closure (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session

### D2. Fetch authenticated CSRF; copy JSON token above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### D3. Optional incorrect-password check (400); account must remain usable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/delete-account
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "password": "intentionally-wrong" }

### D4. Close the disposable account (204, session cookie cleared)
# 409 if it owns a community; nothing is deleted in that case.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/delete-account
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "password": "{{password}}" }

### D5. Former session now denied (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session

### D6. Public author placeholder (200, Deleted user, deleted=true, empty bio)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/participants/{{participantId}}

### D7. Post still readable (200 if otherwise public and unhidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/nodes/{{nodeId}}

### D8. Comments still readable under existing visibility rules
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/nodes/{{nodeId}}/comments

# Fetch a fresh anonymous CSRF before testing failed login or recovery via the other files.
# A new registration with the old email is a new participant; it does not reclaim old contributions.
# Account closure does not scrub names/self-identifying information inside authored post/comment text.
